1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,478
Now the power features.

2
00:00:02,478 --> 00:00:05,350
Delegation, automation, and research.

3
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:05,850
Delegation first.

4
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:12,120
Hermes can spawn isolated sub-agents for parallel
workstreams, so three tasks finish in the time of one.

5
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:22,152
It can also write Python scripts that call its own tools through R P C, collapsing
long multi-step pipelines into a single step that costs almost zero context.

6
00:00:22,152 --> 00:00:23,569
Automation next.

7
00:00:23,569 --> 00:00:34,161
A built-in cron scheduler takes plain-English schedules, like a daily report, a nightly
backup, or a weekly audit, and delivers the result to any platform, fully unattended.

8
00:00:34,161 --> 00:00:35,546
Finally, research.

9
00:00:35,546 --> 00:00:44,586
Hermes supports batch trajectory generation and trajectory compression,
producing training data for the next generation of tool-calling models.

10
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:48,834
Parallel workers, scheduled habits, and a
data flywheel for researchers.

11
00:00:48,834 --> 00:00:50,356
Let us get you installed.

